{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794127241,"nonce":"pA+X0HLt+GLc95RgbwluVdU/314=","title":"Default Linux sans font list starts with Ubuntu, which fontconfig maps to a different family than the next fallback","message":"GitHub issue 69, minor note. LinuxTheme's sans lists (light and dark) and the default typography tokens start with \"Ubuntu\", then \"DejaVu Sans\". On a system without Ubuntu (Fedora, KDE), fontconfig resolves \"Ubuntu\" to some other family (Noto Sans), which can differ from the DejaVu Sans the rest of the fallback chain uses, so text measured and drawn in one place can come from a different font than in another. blinc_text's registry keeps its own Linux list (Cantarell, Ubuntu, Noto Sans, DejaVu Sans), so the two lists disagree.\n\nNeeded: one Linux fallback order shared by the theme and the registry, and a check that a missing first family falls through to the next listed one and not to a fontconfig substitute.","files":null}]}